## Depth-aware IDENT vs fake C args (Decide card)
| | Depth-aware IDENT walk (I1) | Fake C `args` + `c_secret_emit_guard` (I5) |
|--|------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| Input | Lexer toks (`IDENT` field 3) | Joined lowered C text |
| H-same `("x") + tok` | Walk continues at `depth>0`; refuse `tok` | Guard would see `tok` **if** someone built `args` |
| H-later `id(1), tok` | Same | Same, **if** `args` is the **full** list |
| check / llvm / wasm | **This is the rail** | Wrong signature / empty-args FN |
| stmt emit-c | Pre-scan toks **before** `oo_print_*` | Requires concat join Memory forbids |
| eprintln emit-c | Unchanged belt | Already this rail |
| Heap | Token list already paid | **New** `args = args + ", " + a` |
| DE2.9 words | Honest residual: still not a guard call | Theater that **looks** like the sentence |
| Wave-1 | I3 optional DRY, now **required machine** | I5 / I9 **died** |
| Ship this turn | **Yes** | **No** |

**Ship-now decision:** **depth-aware IDENT walk.**
Fake C args are not a 2.9 close. They are a second re-lexer of tokens I1
already walks.

